Migrate the GitHub-runner callback to write the V2 result columns (#848)

Original task: the `execution-runner-callback` Edge Function was the last
writer still using the legacy `result` (JSONB) and `error` (TEXT) columns
inherited from the agent_tasks era. The Command Center read both shapes
via a merged-object fallback in `projectTask`, which caused two writer
shapes to drift and made future schema cleanup harder.

Changes:
- supabase/functions/execution-runner-callback/index.ts now reads and
  writes `execution_result` (JSONB) and `error_code` (TEXT) only. The
  RUNNING / SUCCESS / FAILED branches all merge into the V2 column; the
  prior-state read selects `execution_result` instead of `result`.
- src/pages/DashboardCommandCenter.tsx:
  * Dropped `result` and `error` from `ExecutionTaskRow`.
  * `projectTask` no longer merges legacy + V2; it reads only
    `execution_result` (and `error_code` / `blocked_reason` for the
    error message).
  * Updated the leading comment block to reflect the single-shape model.
- src/lib/execution/dispatchCommandCenter.ts: removed `result,error`
  from `COMMAND_CENTER_TASK_COLUMNS`.
- src/__tests__/lb1-track3-hardening.test.ts: updated `makeRow` and the
  GitHub-runner / FAILED projection tests to use the V2 columns; updated
  the file header comment.
- New migration
  supabase/migrations/20260428100000_execution_runner_callback_v2_backfill.sql:
  one-shot backfill that copies legacy `result` -> `execution_result`
  and `error` -> `error_code` for any row where the V2 columns are
  still empty, so old in-flight rows keep rendering after deploy. The
  DO block is defensive: it no-ops if the legacy columns are already
  dropped.

Verification:
- vitest run src/__tests__/lb1-track3-hardening.test.ts → 21/21 pass.
- tsc --noEmit clean.

Out of scope (not changed):
- src/components/admin/ExecutionTaskPanel.tsx still reads the legacy
  `result` / `error` columns; that component is a separate admin
  surface and the task explicitly scoped only DashboardCommandCenter.

